## Rotating Card – CSS‑only

Below is a minimal, self‑contained example that shows a “card” (a `<div>` with some content) that rotates 180 deg around its Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy‑paste the code into an `.html` file and open it in a browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card</title>
<style>
/* ---------- 1️⃣  Basic reset & layout ---------- */
body{
  display:flex;
  justify-content:center;
  align-items:center;
  height:100vh;
  margin:0;
  background:#f0f0f0;
  font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;
}

/* ---------- 2️⃣  Card container ---------- */
.card{
  width:260px;
  height:160px;
  perspective:800px;          /* gives depth to the 3D effect */
}

/* ---------- 3️⃣  Card inner (the part that actually rotates) ---------- */
.card__inner{
  width:100%;
  height:100%;
  position:relative;
  transition:transform 0.6s ease;
  transform-style:preserve-3d;   /* keep children in 3D space */
}

/* ---------- 4️⃣  Front & back faces ---------- */
.card__face{
  position:absolute;
  width:100%;
  height:100%;
  backface-visibility:hidden;   /* hide the back side when it’s turned away */
  border-radius:12px;
  box-shadow:0 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,.15);
  display:flex;
  justify-content:center;
  align-items:center;
  font-size:1.2rem;
  color:#fff;
}

.card__face--front{
  background:#4a90e2;
}

.card__face--back{
  background:#e94e77;
  transform:rotateY(180deg);   /* start rotated so it’s hidden */
}

/* ---------- 5️⃣  Hover effect ---------- */
.card:hover .card__inner{
  transform:rotateY(180deg);   /* flip the whole card */
}
</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="card">
  <div class="card__inner">
    <div class="card__face card__face--front">
      Front
    </div>
    <div class="card__face card__face--back">
      Back
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens | Why |
|------|--------------|-----|
| **1** | `perspective` on the outer `.card` | Gives the 3D effect; without it the rotation would look flat. |
| **2** | `.card__inner` gets `transform-style: preserve-3d` | Keeps its children (`.card__face`) in 3D space. |
| **3** | `backface-visibility: hidden` on faces | Hides the back side when it’s turned away from the viewer. |
| **4** | `.card__face--back` is pre‑rotated 180° | So when the inner container rotates, the back face becomes visible. |
| **5** | On hover, `.card__inner` rotates 180° | The transition makes it smooth. |

Feel free to replace the text, colors, or add more content inside the faces.  
If you want a different axis (X, Z) or a different rotation angle, just change the `rotateY(180deg)` values accordingly.
